WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.427
Buying Bitcoin takes one tap. Nobody checks whether your plan survives the first crash.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:10.639
Verdict does. Five short steps, three minutes, no account.

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:16.981
Meet Anna. Forty-one, taxed in Slovakia, about to buy her first Bitcoin.

00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:26.510
Savings, pension, retirement, and how long she could live on cash. Her answers stay in her browser, unless she buys the full report.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.102
Home, mortgage, debts. A crash hurts most when something forces you to sell.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.704
Twenty thousand to start, two hundred a month, on her own keys.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.016
And the question most apps never ask: Bitcoin drops seventy percent. What do you do?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.402
Last, what worries her: tax, lost keys, her family never finding it.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.562
Fixed rules, the same for everyone. No AI reads her answers.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:59.276
The Lite score is free, for an email. The full report: fourteen euros, once.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.737
Grade B. Seventy-five out of a hundred. Basics in place.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:10.610
Six areas, scored zero to ten. The weak spots are obvious at a glance.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.751
Then the three things to fix first. Not buy or sell. What to do next.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.558
And every answer read back, so nothing was guessed.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:27.540
The full report explains every point, puts her numbers in euros, and shows her country's tax rule in plain words.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:32.277
Plus a three-step plan for this week, as a PDF she keeps.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:39.412
From there: partners that match her criteria, and a free fifteen-minute call. She compares. She chooses.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.531
Verdict. Check your Bitcoin plan before your money does. Free at Virtuse dot com, slash verdict.
